.Dt STORAGE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm storage
.Nd media penyimpanan, RAID, dan organisasi file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Ini catatan Chapter 10 dari buku Database System Concepts. Isinya:
media penyimpanan fisik, magnetic disk, RAID, tertiary storage,
storage access, file organization, dan data dictionary.
.Pp
Bahasa santai. Tiap konsep dijelasin kenapa dia ada. Karena
database itu hidup di disk. Kalau kamu nggak paham disk, kamu
nggak paham kenapa query bisa lambat atau cepet.
.Ss Bagian 1: Klasifikasi Media Penyimpanan
Media penyimpanan dibedain berdasarkan tiga faktor:
.Bl -tag -width "Reliability" -offset indent
.It Sy Speed
Seberapa cepet data bisa diakses.
.It Sy Cost
Biaya per unit data.
.It Sy Reliability
Ketahanan terhadap power failure atau crash.
.El
.Sy Dua kategori utama:
.Bl -tag -width "Non-volatile" -offset indent
.It Sy Volatile
Isi hilang kalau power mati. Contoh: cache, main memory.
.It Sy Non-volatile
Isi tetap ada walau power mati. Contoh: disk, flash, tape.
.El
.Ss Bagian 2: Physical Storage Media
.Ss Bagian 2.1: Cache
.Sy Paling cepet dan paling mahal.
Volatile. Dikelola hardware komputer, bukan software.
.Ss Bagian 2.2: Main Memory
.Sy Akses cepet
\(em puluhan sampai ratusan nanosecond. Tapi:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Terlalu kecil atau terlalu mahal buat simpen database penuh.
.It
Kapasitas beberapa gigabyte.
.It
Volatile \(em hilang kalau power mati.
.El
.Sy Tren:
Kapasitas naik, biaya per byte turun, kira-kira 2x tiap 2-3 tahun.
.Ss Bagian 2.3: Flash Memory
.Sy Karakteristik:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Data survive power failure.
.It
Data bisa ditulis sekali, tapi lokasi bisa di-erase dan ditulis ulang.
.It
Cuma support 10K \(em 1M write/erase cycles.
.It
Erase harus seluruh bank memory sekaligus.
.It
Read secepat main memory, tapi write lambat (beberapa
microsecond), erase lebih lambat lagi.
.El
.Sy Dipakai di:
Digital camera, phone, USB key.
.Ss Bagian 2.4: Magnetic Disk
.Sy Karakteristik:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Data disimpen di disk yang berputar, dibaca/ditulis magnetically.
.It
Media utama buat long-term storage.
.It
Data harus dipindah ke main memory buat diakses.
.It
Lebih lambat dari main memory.
.It
Direct-access \(em bisa baca di urutan apapun.
.It
Kapasitas sampai ~1.5 TB (tahun 2009).
.It
Survive power failure dan system crash.
.It
Disk failure bisa hancurin data, tapi jarang.
.El
.Ss Bagian 2.5: Optical Storage
.Sy Karakteristik:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Non-volatile, dibaca optik pakai laser dari disk berputar.
.It
CD-ROM (640 MB), DVD (4.7-17 GB), Blu-ray (27-54 GB).
.It
WORM (Write Once Read Many) buat archival: CD-R, DVD-R.
.It
Multiple write versions: CD-RW, DVD-RW, DVD-RAM.
.It
Read/write lebih lambat dari magnetic disk.
.El
.Sy Jukebox systems:
Banyak disk removable, beberapa drive, mekanisme auto-load.
Buat simpen volume data besar.
.Ss Bagian 2.6: Tape Storage
.Sy Karakteristik:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Non-volatile, buat backup dan archival.
.It
Sequential-access \(em jauh lebih lambat dari disk.
.It
Kapasitas tinggi: 40-300 GB per tape.
.It
Tape bisa dilepas dari drive, jadi storage cost lebih murah
dari disk. Tapi drive-nya mahal.
.It
Tape jukebox: ratusan terabyte sampai multiple petabyte.
.El
.Ss Bagian 3: Storage Hierarchy
Hierarki dari yang paling cepet dan mahal ke paling lambat dan
murah:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cache         (paling cepet, paling mahal, volatile)
  |
main memory   (cepet, volatile)
  |
flash memory  (non-volatile, terbatas write cycles)
  |
magnetic disk (non-volatile, kapasitas besar)
  |
optical disk  (non-volatile, lebih lambat)
  |
magnetic tape (non-volatile, sequential, paling murah)
.Ed
.Ss Bagian 3.1: Primary vs Secondary vs Tertiary
.Bl -tag -width "Tertiary" -offset indent
.It Sy Primary storage
Paling cepet tapi volatile. Cache, main memory.
.It Sy Secondary storage
Non-volatile, moderate access time. Juga disebut on-line storage.
Flash, magnetic disk.
.It Sy Tertiary storage
Non-volatile, slow access. Juga disebut off-line storage.
Tape, optical.
.El
.Ss Bagian 4: Magnetic Hard Disk Mechanism
.Sy Komponen:
.Bl -tag -width "Read-write head" -offset indent
.It Sy Platter
Piringan tempat data disimpen.
.It Sy Track
Lingkaran di permukaan platter.
.It Sy Sector
Bagian dari track. Smallest unit of data yang bisa dibaca/ditulis.
.It Sy Cylinder
Track ke-i dari semua platter.
.It Sy Read-write head
Dibaca/ditulis magnetically. Posisinya sangat dekat dengan
platter (hampir nempel).
.It Sy Disk arm
Lengan yang gerakin head ke track yang bener.
.It Sy Spindle
Poros tempat platter berputar.
.El
.Sy Cara baca satu sector:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Disk arm geser ke track yang bener.
.It
Platter berputar terus.
.It
Data dibaca/ditulis pas sector lewat di bawah head.
.El
.Sy Kapasitas:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
50K-100K track per platter.
.It
Sector size 512 byte.
.It
Sector per track: 500-1000 (inner) sampai 1000-2000 (outer).
.It
Head-disk assembly: 1-5 platter per spindle.
.El
.Ss Bagian 4.1: Disk Controller
.Sy Interface antara komputer dan disk drive hardware.
Tugasnya:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Terima high-level command buat baca/tulis sector.
.It
Initiate action \(em gerakin arm, baca/tulis data.
.It
Hitung dan attach checksum ke tiap sector.
.It
Verify write dengan baca balik sector.
.It
Remapping bad sector.
.El
.Sy Checksum:
Kalau data corrupt, dengan high probability stored checksum
nggak match sama recomputed checksum.
.Ss Bagian 4.2: Disk Interface Standards
.Bl -tag -width "SCSI" -offset indent
.It Sy ATA / SATA
AT adaptor, Serial ATA.
.It Sy SCSI / SAS
Small Computer System Interconnect, Serial Attached SCSI.
.It Sy Fiber Channel
FC2Gb atau 4Gb.
.El
.Sy Kecepatan:
SATA 150 MB/s, SATA-II 3Gb (300 MB/s), Ultra 320 SCSI 320 MB/s,
SAS 3-6 Gb/s, FC 256-512 MB/s.
.Ss Bagian 4.3: SAN vs NAS
.Bl -tag -width "NAS" -offset indent
.It Sy SAN (Storage Area Network)
Banyak disk disambung lewat high-speed network ke beberapa
server.
.It Sy NAS (Network Attached Storage)
Networked storage yang provide file system interface pakai
networked file system protocol, bukan disk system interface.
.El
.Ss Bagian 5: Disk Performance
.Ss Bagian 5.1: Access Time
.Sy Waktu dari request issued sampai data transfer mulai.
Terdiri dari:
.Bl -tag -width "Rotational latency" -offset indent
.It Sy Seek time
Waktu buat reposition arm ke track yang bener.
Average = 1/2 worst case. 4-10 ms di disk modern.
.It Sy Rotational latency
Waktu buat sector muncul di bawah head.
Average = 1/2 worst case. 4-11 ms (5400-15000 rpm).
.It Sy Data-transfer rate
Rate data bisa diambil/disimpen. 25-100 MB/s max.
.El
.Ss Bagian 5.2: MTTF (Mean Time To Failure)
.Sy Rata-rata waktu disk jalan tanpa failure.
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Typically 3-5 tahun.
.It
"Theoretical MTTF" 500,000-1,200,000 jam buat disk baru.
.It
MTTF turun seiring umur disk.
.El
.Sy Contoh:
MTTF 1,200,000 jam = kalau kamu punya 1000 disk baru, rata-rata
satu failure tiap 1200 jam.
.Ss Bagian 5.3: Block
.Sy Block
= contiguous sequence of sectors dari satu track.
.Pp
.Sy Ukuran:
512 byte sampai beberapa kilobyte. Typical: 4-16 KB.
.Pp
.Sy Trade-off:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Block kecil: lebih banyak transfer dari disk.
.It
Block besar: lebih banyak space terbuang karena partially
filled block.
.El
.Ss Bagian 5.4: Disk-Arm Scheduling
.Sy Elevator algorithm:
Disk arm gerak satu arah, layanin request sepanjang jalan, terus
balik arah. Minimize arm movement.
.Ss Bagian 6: File Organization
.Sy Optimize block access time
dengan organize block sesuai cara data bakal diakses.
Contoh: simpen related information di cylinder yang sama atau
berdekatan.
.Pp
.Sy Fragmentasi:
Files bisa jadi fragmented seiring waktu. Kalau data di-insert/
delete, atau free block scattered, block dari file baru jadi
scattered juga.
.Pp
.Sy Solusi:
Defragmentation utility.
.Ss Bagian 6.1: Nonvolatile Write Buffers
.Sy Speed up disk writes
dengan nulis block ke non-volatile RAM buffer dulu.
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Non-volatile RAM: battery-backed RAM atau flash memory.
.It
Walau power mati, data aman.
.It
Controller nulis ke disk pas disk nggak ada request lain.
.El
.Sy Log disk:
Disk yang devoted buat nulis sequential log of block updates.
Write ke log disk sangat cepet karena nggak butuh seeks.
.Ss Bagian 6.2: Flash Storage
.Bl -tag -width "NAND flash" -offset indent
.It Sy NOR flash
Lebih mahal.
.It Sy NAND flash
Lebih murah, widely used. Read page-at-a-time (512 byte - 4 KB).
Transfer rate ~20 MB/s.
.It Sy Solid state disks (SSD)
Multiple flash devices, transfer rate 100-200 MB/s.
.El
.Sy Masalah:
Erase lambat (1-2 ms). Erase block contains multiple pages.
.Sy Solusi:
Remapping logical page addresses to physical page addresses.
Translation table track mapping.
.Sy Wear leveling:
Setelah 100,000-1,000,000 erase, erase block unreliable.
.Ss Bagian 7: RAID
.Sy RAID
= Redundant Arrays of Independent Disks.
.Pp
.Sy Tujuan:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
High capacity.
.It
High speed (parallel).
.It
High reliability (redundancy).
.El
.Sy Kenapa perlu?
Chance some disk out of N disks gagal lebih tinggi dari chance
satu disk spesifik gagal. Contoh: 100 disk dengan MTTF 100,000
jam masing-masing \(-> system MTTF 1000 jam (~41 hari).
.Ss Bagian 7.1: Redundancy via Mirroring
.Sy Mirroring (shadowing):
Duplicate setiap disk. Setiap write ke dua disk. Read dari
salah satu.
.Pp
.Sy Data loss:
Cuma kalau disk gagal dan mirror-nya gagal sebelum diperbaiki.
.Pp
.Sy Contoh:
MTTF 100,000 jam, mean time to repair 10 jam \(-> mean time to
data loss 500 juta jam (~57,000 tahun).
.Ss Bagian 7.2: Redundancy via Striping
.Sy Bit-level striping:
Split bits of each byte across multiple disks. 8 disk = 8x rate.
Tapi seek time lebih buruk. Jarang dipakai.
.Pp
.Sy Block-level striping:
Dengan n disk, block ke-i dari file ke disk (i mod n) + 1.
Request buat different block bisa parallel.
.Ss Bagian 7.3: RAID Levels
.Bl -tag -width "RAID 5" -offset indent
.It Sy RAID 0
Block striping, non-redundant. Buat high-performance tapi
data loss nggak critical.
.It Sy RAID 1
Mirrored disks with block striping. Best write performance.
.It Sy RAID 2
Memory-style ECC with bit striping. Jarang dipakai.
.It Sy RAID 3
Bit-interleaved parity. Single parity bit cukup buat error
correction.
.It Sy RAID 4
Block-interleaved parity. Parity block di disk terpisah.
Parity block jadi bottleneck.
.It Sy RAID 5
Block-interleaved distributed parity. Parity disebar di semua
disk. Higher I/O rate dari Level 4.
.It Sy RAID 6
P+Q redundancy. Extra redundant info buat multiple disk failure.
Lebih reliable dari Level 5, tapi lebih mahal.
.El
.Ss Bagian 7.4: Faktor Pemilihan RAID
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Monetary cost.
.It
Performance: I/O per second, bandwidth.
.It
Performance selama failure.
.It
Performance selama rebuild.
.El
.Sy Rekomendasi:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
RAID 0 cuma kalau data safety nggak penting.
.It
RAID 2 dan 4 nggak dipakai (subsumed by 3 dan 5).
.It
RAID 3 nggak dipakai (bit-striping waste disk arm movement).
.It
RAID 6 jarang dipakai (Level 1 dan 5 cukup).
.It
RAID 1 write performance bagus, dipilih buat log disk.
.It
RAID 5 buat low update rate, data besar.
.El
.Ss Bagian 7.5: Hardware Issues
.Bl -tag -width "Hardware RAID" -offset indent
.It Sy Software RAID
Implementasi di software, no special hardware.
.It Sy Hardware RAID
Special hardware. Non-volatile RAM buat record writes.
.El
.Sy Latent failures:
Data yang udah ditulis earlier jadi damaged. Bisa cause data
loss walau cuma satu disk gagal.
.Sy Data scrubbing:
Continually scan for latent failures, recover dari copy/parity.
.Sy Hot swapping:
Replace disk while system running. Reduces recovery time.
.Ss Bagian 8: Tertiary Storage
.Ss Bagian 8.1: Optical Disks
.Bl -tag -width "DVD" -offset indent
.It Sy CD-ROM
640 MB. Seek time ~100 ms. 3000 RPM. 3-6 MB/s.
.It Sy DVD
DVD-5 4.7 GB, DVD-9 8.5 GB, DVD-10 9.4 GB, DVD-18 17 GB.
.It Sy Blu-ray
27 GB, 54 GB double-sided.
.It Sy CD-R / DVD-R
Write once. High capacity, long lifetime. Archival.
.It Sy CD-RW / DVD-RW
Multi-write.
.El
.Ss Bagian 8.2: Tape
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
DAT: few GB. DLT: 10-40 GB. Ultrium: 100+ GB. Ampex: 330 GB.
.It
Transfer rate: few to 10s MB/s.
.It
Tape murah, tapi drive mahal.
.It
Sequential access only.
.It
Tape jukebox: multiple petabyte.
.El
.Ss Bagian 9: File Organization (Record)
.Sy Database disimpen sebagai collection of files.
Setiap file = sequence of records. Record = sequence of fields.
.Ss Bagian 9.1: Fixed-Length Records
.Sy Simple approach:
Simpen record i dari byte n*(i-1), n = ukuran record.
.Pp
.Sy Masalah:
Record bisa cross block boundaries.
.Sy Solusi:
Jangan allow records cross block boundaries.
.Ss Bagian 9.2: Deletion
.Sy Tiga alternatif:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Move records i+1..n ke i..n-1 (compacting).
.It
Move record n ke i (hapus record terakhir).
.It
Jangan move record, link semua free record di free list.
.El
.Sy Free list:
Simpen address record deleted pertama di file header.
Record pertama itu simpen address record deleted kedua, dst.
More space efficient: reuse space atribut normal buat pointers.
.Ss Bagian 9.3: Variable-Length Records
.Sy Kapan terjadi:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Multiple record types dalam satu file.
.It
Record types dengan variable length fields (varchar).
.It
Record types dengan repeating fields.
.El
.Sy Representasi:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Attributes disimpen in order.
.It
Variable length attribute represented by fixed size (offset,
length), actual data stored after all fixed length attributes.
.It
Null values represented by null-value bitmap.
.El
.Ss Bagian 9.4: Slotted Page Structure
.Sy Header berisi:
.Bl -bullet -offset indent
.It
Number of record entries.
.It
End of free space in block.
.It
Location and size of each record.
.El
.Sy Records bisa digerakin dalam page
buat keep contiguous. Entry di header harus diupdate.
.Pp
.Sy Pointers
nggak boleh point langsung ke record. Harus point ke entry
untuk record di header.
.Ss Bagian 9.5: Organisasi Record
.Bl -tag -width "Hashing" -offset indent
.It Sy Heap
Record ditaruh di mana aja yang ada space.
.It Sy Sequential
Record disimpen in order berdasarkan search key.
.It Sy Hashing
Hash function dihitung dari atribut. Hasilnya nentuin block.
.It Sy Multitable clustering
Record dari beberapa relation disimpen di file yang sama.
Motif: minimize I/O dengan simpen related records di block sama.
.El
.Ss Bagian 9.6: Sequential File Organization
.Sy Cocok buat:
Aplikasi yang butuh sequential processing seluruh file.
.Pp
.Sy Deletion:
Pakai pointer chains.
.Pp
.Sy Insertion:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Cari posisi yang tepat.
.It
Kalau ada free space, insert di situ.
.It
Kalau nggak ada, insert di overflow block.
.It
Update pointer chain.
.El
.Sy Reorganize:
Dari waktu ke waktu, restore sequential order.
.Ss Bagian 9.7: Multitable Clustering
.Sy Simpen beberapa relation di satu file.
Contoh: department dan instructor.
.Pp
.Sy Bagus buat:
Query yang involve join department dan instructor.
.Pp
.Sy Jelek buat:
Query yang cuma involve department.
.Pp
.Sy Hasil:
Variable size records. Bisa tambah pointer chains buat link
record dari relation tertentu.
.Ss Bagian 10: Data Dictionary
.Sy Data dictionary (system catalog)
simpen metadata \(em data tentang data.
.Pp
.Sy Isinya:
.Bl -tag -width "Statistik" -offset indent
.It Sy Informasi tentang relation
Nama relation, nama/tipe/length atribut, nama/definisi view,
integrity constraint.
.It Sy User dan accounting
Including password.
.It Sy Statistik dan deskriptif
Jumlah tuple per relation.
.It Sy Physical file organization
Bagaimana relation disimpen (sequential/hash/...).
.It Sy Physical location
Lokasi relation.
.It Sy Informasi tentang index
.El
.Ss Bagian 10.1: Representasi Relational
.Sy Di disk:
Relational representation.
.Sy Di memory:
Specialized data structures buat efficient access.
.Pp
.Sy Contoh tabel metadata:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Relation_metadata:
  relation_name, number_of_attributes,
  storage_organization, location

Attribute_metadata:
  relation_name, attribute_name,
  domain_type, position, length

Index_metadata:
  index_name, relation_name,
  index_type, index_attributes

User_metadata:
  user_name, encrypted_password, group

View_metadata:
  view_name, definition
.Ed
.Ss Bagian 11: Storage Access
.Sy Block
= fixed-length storage unit. Unit of storage allocation dan
data transfer.
.Pp
.Sy Tujuan database system:
Minimize jumlah block transfer antara disk dan memory.
Caranya: keep sebanyak mungkin block di main memory.
.Ss Bagian 11.1: Buffer Manager
.Bl -tag -width "Buffer manager" -offset indent
.It Sy Buffer
Portion of main memory available buat simpen copy of disk block.
.It Sy Buffer manager
Subsystem yang allocate buffer space di main memory.
.El
.Sy Algoritma:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Kalau block udah di buffer, return address-nya.
.It
Kalau belum:
.Bl -enun -offset indent
.It
Allocate space. Replace block lain kalau perlu.
.It
Replaced block ditulis balik ke disk hanya kalau dimodif.
.It
Baca block dari disk ke buffer.
.It
Return address ke requester.
.El
.El
.Ss Bagian 11.2: Replacement Strategy
.Bl -tag -width "Toss-immediate" -offset indent
.It Sy LRU (Least Recently Used)
Ganti block yang paling lama nggak diakses.
.Idea:
Use past pattern sebagai predictor future.
.It Sy MRU (Most Recently Used)
System pin block yang sedang diproses. Setelah selesai,
block unpinned dan jadi MRU.
.It Sy Toss-immediate
Free space block begitu tuple terakhir diproses.
.El
.Sy Kenapa LRU bisa jelek?
Buat query yang repeated scan (nested loop join), LRU bisa
ganti block yang baru aja dipakai, padahal besok dipakai lagi.
.Sy Solusi:
Mixed strategy dengan hints dari query optimizer.
.Ss Bagian 11.3: Pinned Block
.Sy Block di memory yang nggak boleh ditulis balik ke disk.
.Pp
.Sy Contoh:
Block yang sedang diproses, atau block yang lagi di-update.
.Ss Ringkasan
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Konsep                Inti
Volatile              Hilang kalau power mati
Non-volatile          Tetap ada
Cache                 Paling cepet, volatile
Main memory           Cepet, volatile
Flash memory          Non-volatile, write terbatas
Magnetic disk         Non-volatile, direct access
Optical disk          Non-volatile, laser
Tape                  Non-volatile, sequential
Primary storage       Cache + main memory
Secondary storage     Flash + disk
Tertiary storage      Tape + optical
Track                 Lingkaran di platter
Sector                Smallest unit of data
Cylinder              Track ke-i dari semua platter
Seek time             Waktu reposition arm
Rotational latency    Waktu sector muncul
MTTF                  Mean time to failure
Block                 Contiguous sectors
RAID                  Redundant array of independent disks
Mirroring             Duplicate disk
Striping              Split data across disks
Parity                Redundancy via XOR
Fixed-length record   Record dengan ukuran tetap
Variable-length       Record dengan ukuran berubah
Slotted page          Page dengan slot header
Heap                  Record di mana aja
Sequential            Record in order
Hashing               Hash function
Multitable clustering Simpen beberapa relation
Data dictionary       Metadata
Buffer                Portion of memory
Buffer manager        Allocate buffer space
LRU                   Least recently used
Pinned block          Block nggak boleh ditulis
.Ed
Kalau kamu cuma inget satu hal dari catatan ini, inget ini:
.Sy disk itu lambat, memory itu cepet.
Semua teknik di chapter ini \(em caching, buffering, RAID,
clustering \(em tujuannya satu: minimize jumlah kali kamu
harus nyentuh disk.
.Pp
Yang belum dijawab di sini: gimana caranya database nentuin
block mana yang perlu di-cache? Kapan pakai LRU, kapan pakai
MRU? Gimana caranya recovery kalau disk failure? Itu topik
lanjutan: buffer replacement policy, recovery. Kalau
penasaran, cari sendiri.
